Reason: SpatialGrid_syncGrid took each moved instance out of its old cells one at a time, searching and shifting
each cell once per mover; a mine chain's projectiles crowd the same cells (~1,150 movers a frame at its peak). The
movers' old cells are now each compacted once, a cell entry being dropped when it is a mover and the cell is one of
that mover's old cells (the cells the one-at-a-time removal looked in); movers are found by address in a hash table,
so no instance memory is read per cell entry. Movers are then appended in the same order as before, so every cell
and every instance's cell list ends up exactly as the one-at-a-time sync left them.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

--- a/src/spatial_grid.c
